      "message": "Hi maintainers,\n\nCould you review this change to suppress redundant Value signals\nafter repeated GetSensorReading response decode failures?\n\nupdateReading() already skips Value assignments when both the\ncurrent and new readings are NaN. Decode failures instead call\nhandleErrGetSensorReading(), which previously assigned NaN\nunconditionally. Since NaN compares unequal to itself, the\ngenerated setter emits PropertiesChanged on every assignment.\n\nThe new checks cover both Sensor.Value and Metric.Value. They\npreserve the first transition from a finite or infinite value to\nNaN, continue marking the sensor non-functional, and leave\nrecovery notifications unchanged.",
